---
description: Routes any documentation task to the correct skill file. Always active.
alwaysApply: true
---

The Task - Skill table and all repo-wide rules are in `AGENTS.md` at the repo root. It is the single source of truth.

When the user gives you a task:

1. Translate the request to English internally.
2. Match it to a skill using the table in `AGENTS.md`.
3. Open the skill file with a Read tool call before writing any response.
4. Follow the skill file exactly. Do only what it says. Do not add a component, attribute, section, sentence, link, file, or step it does not name. If it is silent, stop and ask. See `.cursor/rules/follow-skill-exactly.mdc`.
5. After the main task is finished, run the What's new triage in `AGENTS.md`. That is the only second skill in the same session. A task that names several articles is still one task: keep every article on the branch the task already has.
